From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] cellGcm: NV0039 copies other than the frame chain run with
 the GPU MLAA

With PS3RECOMP_MLAA_GPU=1 (the default through KZ_MLAA=gpu) and
PS3RECOMP_NV0039 off, every NV0039 copy was dropped, not only the two of
Killzone HD's frame chain (FUN_001109E8: the 1280x720x4 frame out to main
memory, where the GPU MLAA runs, and the SPUs' result back). When the
VICTORY, FAILED or pause screen opens, the game (FUN_00273F00) makes a
local texture the size of the draw target (renderer +0x60), copies the
target into it with an NV0039 copy (FUN_002FE3EC -> FUN_0031BB58) and
func_0029BDC8 draws it full screen, tinted through a 256x1 palette, as the
screen's background. Without the copy the texture kept what the memory
held: zeros early in a session (a flat dark green, as on the PS3), and
after a few levels a later level's data (an F12 capture of 2026-11-08: the
texture at local 0x0CDE0000 held big-endian floats), drawn as coloured
noise and tinted green (issue: the menus' background stays grainy in long
sessions).

gcm_nv0039_route() decides: with PS3RECOMP_NV0039 on, everything is copied
as before; otherwise only the frame chain's two copies (1280x720x4 bytes in
one line between local and main memory) go to the GPU MLAA or are dropped,
and every other copy runs, reading the source back from the GPU first as
patch 2035's copies do.
---
diff --git a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
index fedab6e..0235d38 100644
--- a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
+++ b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ static u32 s_gcm_context_ea = 0;
 #include <time.h>
 #endif
 #include "gcm_flip_wait.h"   /* PS3_GCM_MAX_QUEUED_FLIPS's wait */
+#include "gcm_nv0039_route.h" /* which NV0039 copies run (patch 2059) */
 
 /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Timestamp helpers (same pattern as sys_timer)
@@ -1525,8 +1526,11 @@ static void nv0039_copy(const u32* r)
     }
     const u32 loc_in  = s_nv0039.dma_in  == 0xFEED0001u ? RSX_LOCATION_MAIN : RSX_LOCATION_LOCAL;
     const u32 loc_out = s_nv0039.dma_out == 0xFEED0001u ? RSX_LOCATION_MAIN : RSX_LOCATION_LOCAL;
-    if (mlaa_gpu_enabled()) {
-        if (loc_in == RSX_LOCATION_LOCAL && loc_out == RSX_LOCATION_MAIN && len == 1280u * 720u * 4u && lines == 1u) {
+    const int route = gcm_nv0039_route(nv0039_enabled(), mlaa_gpu_enabled(), loc_in == RSX_LOCATION_MAIN,
+                                       loc_out == RSX_LOCATION_MAIN, len, lines);
+    if (route == NV0039_ROUTE_DROP) return;
+    if (route == NV0039_ROUTE_MLAA) {
+        {
             /* PS3RECOMP_MB_GPU=<IO offset>: the 640x360 main-memory target there
              * is the title's motion field, and its motion blur follows the MLAA */
             static u32 mb = 0;
diff --git a/libs/video/gcm_nv0039_route.h b/libs/video/gcm_nv0039_route.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d2f938f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libs/video/gcm_nv0039_route.h
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+/*
+ * What an NV0039 (memory to memory) copy becomes, by the switches and its
+ * shape. Header-only so a host test can check it without the GCM state.
+ *
+ * Killzone HD's frame chain (FUN_001109E8) moves the whole finished frame,
+ * 1280x720x4 bytes as one line, between a local display buffer and main
+ * memory, out and back. Those two are the only copies that need the SPU chain
+ * (PS3RECOMP_NV0039=1) or that the GPU MLAA (PS3RECOMP_MLAA_GPU=1) takes
+ * over. Every other copy is a plain copy the title relies on: when a screen
+ * opens (VICTORY, FAILED, pause; FUN_00273F00), the game copies the current
+ * draw target into a new local texture (local to local, FUN_002FE3EC) and
+ * draws it tinted as the screen's background (func_0029BDC8). With the MLAA
+ * on the GPU that copy was dropped as well, so the texture kept whatever the
+ * memory held: zeros early in a session (a flat background), a later level's
+ * data after a few levels (a grainy one).
+ */
+#ifndef PS3RECOMP_GCM_NV0039_ROUTE_H
+#define PS3RECOMP_GCM_NV0039_ROUTE_H
+
+enum { NV0039_ROUTE_COPY, NV0039_ROUTE_MLAA, NV0039_ROUTE_DROP };
+
+/* loc_*: 0 local, 1 main (RSX_LOCATION_*). */
+static inline int gcm_nv0039_route(int nv0039_on, int mlaa_gpu, unsigned loc_in, unsigned loc_out,
+                                   unsigned len, unsigned lines)
+{
+    if (nv0039_on) return NV0039_ROUTE_COPY;
+    const int frame_chain = len == 1280u * 720u * 4u && lines == 1u && loc_in != loc_out;
+    if (!frame_chain) return NV0039_ROUTE_COPY;
+    /* the frame out to main memory: the GPU MLAA; the SPUs' result back: dropped */
+    return mlaa_gpu && loc_in == 0u && loc_out == 1u ? NV0039_ROUTE_MLAA : NV0039_ROUTE_DROP;
+}
+#endif
